    "wool": {
      "type": "aa-text-media",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Teotitlán del Valle · Wool",
        "heading": "Woven on the pedal loom",
        "heading_size": "h2",
        "body": "<p>A family weaving workshop works on the pedal loom: feet set the warp, hands pass the shuttle. Patterns are kept in memory or lightly sketched, so even with the same design, no two pieces are identical.</p><p>Every colour is naturally dyed: reds and pinks from cochineal, blues from indigo, yellows and oranges from pericón and marigold, browns from walnut.</p>",
        "button_label": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "button_style": "button-secondary",
        "image": "",
        "shape": "vase-wide",
        "image_side": "right",
        "media_width": "medium",
        "caption": "Wool on the pedal loom",
        "place": "Teotitlán del Valle",
